<title>FRANCE: France says Daewoo to create French jobs.</title>
<headline>France says Daewoo to create French jobs.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French prime minister's office said on Wednesday that Daewoo Electronics had agreed to preserve French jobs and create additional ones as part of the terms for a buyout of Thomson Multimedia (TMM).</p>
<p>TMM is a wholly owned unit of state-owned Thomson SA, which the government wants to sell to missiles-to-magazines conglomerate Lagardere Group.</p>
<p>The government announced on Wednesday that it preferred Lagardere's bid, which envisages the sale of TMM to Daewoo, over a rival offer from Alcatel Alsthom.</p>
<p>The prime minister's office said in a statement that Daewoo, &quot;already recognised as a major investor in France&quot;, would help TMM develop the competitiveness needed to ensure its future.</p>
<p>&quot;Daewoo Electronics' offer entails a commitment to preserve Thomson Multimedia jobs in France and create additional jobs in the country,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Lagardere will focus on a merger of its missiles activities with Thomson's defence electronics operations.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom, +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
